# Environment for {{.Project}} (generated by unmute).
# Copy this file to `.env` and fill in the values. Never commit `.env`.
#
{{if .DailyCarrier}}# Only what you supply. The Daily helper's public URL is one
# of those values because you host it; its exact URL is part of carrier signature
# validation. compile-report.json lists every name the project needs.
{{else}}# Only what you supply. Anything the route supplies for you — Redis, the public
# URL, the outbound token — is not here, because it is not yours to set:
# `unmute dev` supplies it for a local run, and your platform or operator
# supplies it at deploy time. compile-report.json lists every name the project
# needs, including those.{{end}}
{{if .DailyCarrier}}
# agent side: the deployed agent reads these, so they belong in the platform
# secret set.
{{range .DailyCarrier.AgentEnv}}{{.}}=
{{end}}
# helper side: telephony_helper.py reads these where you run it. The deployed
# agent reads none of them, so leave them out of the platform secret set.
{{range .DailyCarrier.HelperEnv}}{{.}}=
{{end}}
# shared: telephony_helper.py also reads {{.DailyCarrier.AuthTokenEnv}} above to
# verify the carrier signature. Keep it in the platform secret set because the
# deployed agent uses the same credential to forward the existing phone leg.
# helper side, optional: unset is fine. With no hold audio the caller hears a
# spoken line instead, and with no room geography Daily picks its own.
{{range .DailyCarrier.OptionalEnv}}# {{.}}=
{{end}}{{else}}{{if and .CloudWebsocket .CloudWebsocket.CallEnv}}
# One group, because one thing reads them: the deployed agent. There is no second
# side on this route, so every name here belongs in the platform secret set.
#
# What a phone call adds: {{join .CloudWebsocket.CallEnv ", "}}.
# Your carrier's credentials and caller identity, plus the platform's name for
# your organization. A package that only receives calls on this route needs none
# of them, and a browser or console session never reads them.
{{end}}
{{range .AuthorEnv}}{{.}}=
{{end}}{{end}}
